IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tas-nouns`
IMPORT `tas-provisions`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1931 (Tasmania): the defined terms, as data.
-- One row for each defined term of the text: where it is defined, where its definition applies (the Act's own words), how the Act words it,
-- the Act's words, and the other instruments the definition points at.
-- The rows are written by a script that reads the text file; the quotation above each row is the text itself.
-- Where a definition needs more than a row, the rule is in the module for its section (see NOTES.md).

-- src:29 | regulation includes rule and by-law.
@ref s 2A regulation (src:29)
`defined term: regulation (s 2A)` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "regulation", "s 2A", "In this Act", `worded as an inclusion`, "regulation includes rule and by-law.", ""

-- src:67 | Act used in relation to a legislative enactment, shall include all Acts and ordinances which have been duly made and passed by the Parliament of Tasmania or by any council or authority empowered to make and pass laws in Tasmania, and to which assent has been duly given by or on behalf of the Sovereign.
@ref s 5(1) Act (src:67)
`defined term: Act (s 5(1))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "Act", "s 5(1)", "", `worded as an inclusion`, "Act used in relation to a legislative enactment, shall include all Acts and ordinances which have been duly made and passed by the Parliament of Tasmania or by any council or authority empowered to make and pass laws in Tasmania, and to which assent has been duly given by or on behalf of the Sovereign.", ""

-- src:95 | In any Act, the expression prescribed –
-- src:97 | (a) means prescribed by, or by regulations made under, the Act in which the word appears; and
-- src:99 | (b) where reference is made to anything prescribed by an Act other than the Act in which the word appears, includes anything prescribed by any regulation made under that other Act.
@ref s 7 prescribed (src:95-99)
`defined term: prescribed (s 7)` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "prescribed", "s 7", "In any Act", `worded as a closed meaning`, "In any Act, the expression prescribed – (a) means prescribed by, or by regulations made under, the Act in which the word appears; and (b) where reference is made to anything prescribed by an Act other than the Act in which the word appears, includes anything prescribed by any regulation made under that other Act.", ""

-- src:117 | the Principal Act in any such amending Act, unless the contrary is expressly provided, shall mean the Act so amended, and shall be deemed to apply to the earliest of the series of Acts upon the same subject, even though the amendment consists only of some alteration in, or modification of, a previous amending Act.
@ref s 8(2) the Principal Act (src:117)
`defined term: the Principal Act (s 8(2))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "the Principal Act", "s 8(2)", "", `worded as a closed meaning`, "the Principal Act in any such amending Act, unless the contrary is expressly provided, shall mean the Act so amended, and shall be deemed to apply to the earliest of the series of Acts upon the same subject, even though the amendment consists only of some alteration in, or modification of, a previous amending Act.", ""

-- src:145 | extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act, means material not forming part of the Act, including –
-- src:147 | (a) material that is set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer; and
-- src:149 | (b) a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission or Commissioner, board or committee of inquiry, or a similar body, that was laid before either House of Parliament before the provision concerned was enacted; and
-- src:151 | (c) a relevant report of a committee of Parliament or of either House of Parliament that was made to Parliament or that House of Parliament before the provision was enacted; and
-- src:153 | (d) a treaty or other international agreement that is mentioned in the Act; and
-- src:155 | (e) any explanatory note, clause note or memorandum relating to the Bill that contained the provision, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or given or otherwise made available to the members of, either House of Parliament by the member bringing in the Bill before the provision was enacted; and
-- src:157 | (f) the speech made to a House of Parliament by a member of the House in moving a motion that the Bill be read a second time; and
-- src:159 | (g) relevant material in the Votes and Proceedings of either House of Parliament or in any official record of debates in Parliament or either House of Parliament; and
-- src:161 | (h) a document that is declared by an Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section;
@ref s 8B(3) extrinsic material (src:145-161)
`defined term: extrinsic material (s 8B(3))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "extrinsic material", "s 8B(3)", "In this section", `worded as a closed meaning`, "extrinsic material in relation to a provision of an Act, means material not forming part of the Act, including – (a) material that is set out in the document containing the text of the Act as printed by the Government Printer; and (b) a relevant report of a Royal Commission, Law Reform Commission or Commissioner, board or committee of inquiry, or a similar body, that was laid before either House of Parliament before the provision concerned was enacted; and (c) a relevant report of a committee of Parliament or of either House of Parliament that was made to Parliament or that House of Parliament before the provision was enacted; and (d) a treaty or other international agreement that is mentioned in the Act; and (e) any explanatory note, clause note or memorandum relating to the Bill that contained the provision, or any other relevant document, that was laid before, or given or otherwise made available to the members of, either House of Parliament by the member bringing in the Bill before the provision was enacted; and (f) the speech made to a House of Parliament by a member of the House in moving a motion that the Bill be read a second time; and (g) relevant material in the Votes and Proceedings of either House of Parliament or in any official record of debates in Parliament or either House of Parliament; and (h) a document that is declared by an Act to be a relevant document for the purposes of this section;", ""

-- src:163 | ordinary meaning means the ordinary meaning conveyed by a provision having regard to its context in the Act and to the purpose or object of the Act.
@ref s 8B(3) ordinary meaning (src:163)
`defined term: ordinary meaning (s 8B(3))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "ordinary meaning", "s 8B(3)", "In this section", `worded as a closed meaning`, "ordinary meaning means the ordinary meaning conveyed by a provision having regard to its context in the Act and to the purpose or object of the Act.", ""

-- src:433 | appointing authority, in relation to an office, position or appointment, means –
-- src:435 | (a) in the case of an office, position or appointment to which appointments are required by or under an enactment to be made by the Governor – the Minister administering that enactment; and
-- src:437 | (b) in any other case – the person by whom appointments to that office, position or appointment are authorized to be made;
@ref s 21A(2) appointing authority (src:433-437)
`defined term: appointing authority (s 21A(2))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "appointing authority", "s 21A(2)", "In this section", `worded as a closed meaning`, "appointing authority, in relation to an office, position or appointment, means – (a) in the case of an office, position or appointment to which appointments are required by or under an enactment to be made by the Governor – the Minister administering that enactment; and (b) in any other case – the person by whom appointments to that office, position or appointment are authorized to be made;", ""

-- src:439 | eligible person, in relation to an office, position or appointment, means a person who possesses the qualifications required by law to be possessed by the holder of that office, position or appointment;
@ref s 21A(2) eligible person (src:439)
`defined term: eligible person (s 21A(2))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "eligible person", "s 21A(2)", "In this section", `worded as a closed meaning`, "eligible person, in relation to an office, position or appointment, means a person who possesses the qualifications required by law to be possessed by the holder of that office, position or appointment;", ""

-- src:441 | enactment means –
-- src:443 | (a) an Act; or
-- src:445 | (b) any other instrument of a legislative character; or
-- src:447 | (c) any provision of an Act or of an instrument referred to in paragraph (b).
@ref s 21A(2) enactment (src:441-447)
`defined term: enactment (s 21A(2))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "enactment", "s 21A(2)", "In this section", `worded as a closed meaning`, "enactment means – (a) an Act; or (b) any other instrument of a legislative character; or (c) any provision of an Act or of an instrument referred to in paragraph (b).", ""

-- src:597 | (3) Where any time, or the first or last day (according as it is reckoned backwards or forwards) of any period of time, prescribed or allowed for the doing of any act or thing falls on a Sunday or on any day which is a statutory holiday as defined in the Statutory Holidays Act 2000 or a public holiday throughout the State or in that part of the State where the act or thing is to be, or may be, done (which days are in this section referred to as excluded days) the act or thing –
@ref s 29(3) excluded days (src:597)
`defined term: excluded days (s 29(3))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "excluded days", "s 29(3)", "in this section", `worded as a closed meaning`, "(3) Where any time, or the first or last day (according as it is reckoned backwards or forwards) of any period of time, prescribed or allowed for the doing of any act or thing falls on a Sunday or on any day which is a statutory holiday as defined in the Statutory Holidays Act 2000 or a public holiday throughout the State or in that part of the State where the act or thing is to be, or may be, done (which days are in this section referred to as excluded days) the act or thing –", "Statutory Holidays Act 2000"

-- src:615 | Commonwealth Act means the National Measurement Act 1960 of the Commonwealth, and includes that Act as amended from time to time and any Commonwealth Act passed in substitution for that Act;
@ref s 29A(2) Commonwealth Act (src:615)
`defined term: Commonwealth Act (s 29A(2))` MEANS
    `Defined term` OF "Commonwealth Act", "s 29A(2)", "In this section", `worded as a closed meaning`, "Commonwealth Act means the National Measurement Act 1960 of the Commonwealth, and includes that Act as amended from time to time and any Commonwealth Act passed in substitution for that Act;", "National Measurement Act 1960 (Commonwealth)"

-- src:617 | Commonwealth legal unit of measurement means a unit of measurement prescribed under the Commonwealth Act.
